{
  "name": "Day 57 Solution: AI Agents Capstone Review",
  "description": "A 3-workflow capstone system (intake, decision, reporting) chained via HTTP calls to each workflow's own production webhook, plus a maintenance health-check layer and a Day 53-style batching/throttling scaling layer, all represented in one importable file.",
  "tags": ["week8", "ai-agents", "capstone"],
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "overview-sticky",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [140, 20],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Day 57 Solution: AI Agents Capstone Review\n\nThis single importable file represents a 3-workflow production system: Intake → Process/Decision → Reporting, chained the way 3 separately-deployed n8n workflows would call each other's production webhooks, plus a maintenance health-check layer (Day 52) and a batched/throttled scaling layer (Day 53) on the intake side.\n\n**Credentials needed to run for real:** OpenAI API key. None needed to inspect the structure.\n\nSee DAILY_TASKS/DAY_57_AI_Agents_Capstone_Review.md for the full task.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 460
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "section-intake-sticky",
      "name": "Section: Workflow 1 Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [180, 560],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Workflow 1: Intake (+ Scaling Layer)\n\nAccepts `{\"items\":[...]}`, validates it's a non-empty array, then batches items 5-at-a-time through Split In Batches with a throttling Wait before each call to Workflow 2 — the same pattern as the Day 53 solution, applied here to the capstone's entry point so a 10+ item payload doesn't overwhelm the chain.",
        "height": 200,
        "width": 340
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "capstone-intake-webhook",
      "name": "Capstone Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [240, 400],
      "parameters": {
        "path": "capstone-intake",
        "httpMethod": "POST"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "validate-intake-input",
      "name": "Validate Intake Input",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [490, 400],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "cond-items-nonempty-array",
              "leftValue": "={{ Array.isArray($json.items) && $json.items.length > 0 }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "intake-validation-error",
      "name": "Intake Validation Error",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [740, 620],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "status",
              "value": "error"
            },
            {
              "name": "message",
              "value": "Request must include a non-empty 'items' array."
            },
            {
              "name": "workflow",
              "value": "AI Capstone System - Intake"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "init-intake-batch",
      "name": "Init Intake Batch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [740, 400],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "intake_id",
              "value": "={{ $now.format('yyyyLLddHHmmss') }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "items",
              "value": "={{ $json.items }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "total_item_count",
              "value": "={{ $json.items.length }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "batch_start_time",
              "value": "={{ $now }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "intake-split-in-batches",
      "name": "Intake Split In Batches",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitInBatches",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [990, 400],
      "parameters": {
        "batchSize": 5,
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "intake-throttle-wait",
      "name": "Intake Throttle Wait",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wait",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [1240, 560],
      "parameters": {
        "amount": 2,
        "unit": "seconds"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "call-workflow2-process",
      "name": "Call Workflow 2: Process (placeholder)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [1490, 560],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://your-n8n-instance.example.com/webhook/capstone-process",
        "sendBody": true,
        "bodyContentType": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ { \"intake_id\": $('Init Intake Batch').item.json.intake_id, \"batch_item\": $json } }}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "synthesize-decision",
      "name": "Synthesize Decision",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.openAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [1240, 240],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "chat",
        "operation": "create",
        "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You are Workflow 2's decision-making agent. All batches have been sent on to processing. Produce one short overall decision/recommendation for the whole intake batch."
            },
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "={{ 'Intake ID: ' + $json.intake_id + '\\nTotal items processed: ' + $json.total_item_count }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.3,
          "maxTokens": 400
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "section-process-sticky",
      "name": "Section: Workflows 2 & 3 (placeholder)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1490, 20],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ⚠️ Workflow 2 & 3: Chained Webhooks (placeholder)\n\nIn real use, Workflow 2 (Process/Decision) and Workflow 3 (Reporting) would be two **separately deployed, separately Active** n8n workflows, each with its own production webhook. This file simulates that chain with HTTP Request calls to placeholder URLs (`.../webhook/capstone-process`, `.../webhook/capstone-report`) — replace them with your real Day 51-style production URLs once all 3 workflows are actually deployed.\n\nThe **Synthesize Decision** OpenAI node stands in for the AI logic that would live inside Workflow 2.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 400
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "call-workflow3-report",
      "name": "Call Workflow 3: Report (placeholder)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [1490, 240],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://your-n8n-instance.example.com/webhook/capstone-report",
        "sendBody": true,
        "bodyContentType": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ { \"intake_id\": $('Init Intake Batch').item.json.intake_id, \"decision\": $json.choices[0].message.content, \"total_item_count\": $('Init Intake Batch').item.json.total_item_count } }}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "final-system-report",
      "name": "Final System Report",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [1740, 240],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "intake_id",
              "value": "={{ $('Init Intake Batch').item.json.intake_id }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "total_items",
              "value": "={{ $('Init Intake Batch').item.json.total_item_count }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "ai_decision",
              "value": "={{ $('Synthesize Decision').item.json.choices[0].message.content }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "reporting_status",
              "value": "sent_to_workflow_3"
            },
            {
              "name": "completed_at",
              "value": "={{ $now.toISO() }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "section-maintenance-sticky",
      "name": "Section: Maintenance Layer",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [180, 780],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Maintenance Layer (Day 52 pattern)\n\nA separate Schedule Trigger health-checks all 3 chained production webhooks (Intake, Process, Report) and aggregates one combined health report — the same pattern as the Day 52 solution, extended to 3 targets instead of 1.",
        "height": 160,
        "width": 340
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "capstone-health-schedule",
      "name": "Capstone Health Check Schedule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [240, 980],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "health-check-intake",
      "name": "Health Check: Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [520, 880],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://your-n8n-instance.example.com/webhook/capstone-intake",
        "sendBody": true,
        "bodyContentType": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ { \"items\": [ { \"text\": \"health-check ping\" } ] } }}",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "json"
            }
          },
          "timeout": 10000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "health-check-process",
      "name": "Health Check: Process",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [520, 980],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://your-n8n-instance.example.com/webhook/capstone-process",
        "sendBody": true,
        "bodyContentType": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ { \"ping\": true } }}",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "json"
            }
          },
          "timeout": 10000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "health-check-report",
      "name": "Health Check: Report",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [520, 1080],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://your-n8n-instance.example.com/webhook/capstone-report",
        "sendBody": true,
        "bodyContentType": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ { \"ping\": true } }}",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "json"
            }
          },
          "timeout": 10000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "aggregate-health-report",
      "name": "Aggregate Health Report",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [780, 980],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "name": "combined_health_report",
              "value": "={{ { \"intake\": $('Health Check: Intake').item.json, \"process\": $('Health Check: Process').item.json, \"report\": $('Health Check: Report').item.json } }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "checked_at",
              "value": "={{ $now.toISO() }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "system-status-sticky",
      "name": "System Status",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [990, 780],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## System Status\n\n**Deployed:** 3 chained workflows (Intake, Process/Decision, Reporting), each intended to run Active with its own production webhook, called via HTTP Request the way separately-deployed n8n workflows chain together.\n\n**Monitored:** A Schedule Trigger health-checks all 3 production webhooks hourly and aggregates one combined health report (maintenance layer, Day 52 pattern).\n\n**Documented:** Every section carries a Sticky Note explaining its role; the input/output contracts follow the same shape established in the Day 51/54/56 solutions.\n\n**Real gaps before client handoff:**\n1. **No real authentication on the chained webhooks** — anyone who guesses/finds the URLs can call them; production would need header-based auth or n8n's built-in webhook authentication.\n2. **No persistent logging store** — the audit trail relies on n8n's own execution history rather than an external log (Google Sheets/Airtable/DB), so history is lost if executions are pruned.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 460
      }
    }
  ],
